100% Meat Machine Post, handcrafted for you (I personally typed in the emdash)!<p>site: &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev</a>&gt;
quickstart: &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;docs&#x2F;quickstart" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;docs&#x2F;quickstart</a>&gt;
examples: &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;apps" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;apps</a>&gt;   &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;games" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;games</a>&gt; &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;examples" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;examples</a>&gt;
arch: &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;arch" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;arch</a>&gt;
dsl: &lt;<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;dsl" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;statebase.dev&#x2F;dsl</a>&gt;<p>Hi everyone, I&#x27;m Brian. I like frontend a lot. I can do backend, but not every little thing is worth it and I&#x27;ve been making &quot;detached&quot; HTML apps (not even needing a web server) as long as I can remember. I wanted a way to standup some sort of secure way to save data, maybe with a little bit of logic with just a few commands. I didn&#x27;t want code (TypeScript, Java, C#, etc), but I also didn&#x27;t want no code either -- maybe it&#x27;s the devops in me (Terraform?). I was done waiting, and made this. It hosts the logic, permissions and state you need for an agent, application or game with pure curl commands. Thousands of jobless engineers and &quot;learn backend or die&quot; attitude why should backend have all the fun? Besides this might be good for scripting and infrastructure setup too, so it has something for everyone. There&#x27;s also a Tauri+pglite version for desktop dev (thank you pglite) and a Devvit template for Reddit games (I made a couple, ask) all running on the same engine.<p>Please give it a shot, and if you like what you see join my team (I got tired of working on it alone so I added a childhood friend and a few ex-coworkers) and I in our Discord. I&#x27;m full time on it now so any feedback even negative is more fuel. If it sucks, we want to know about it, so we can make it better.<p>Now for the big questions<p>*Is it Open Source?*<p>Not yet. There&#x27;s a lot of reasons but the main one is the code is in a giant monorepo that has to be cleaned up. Another reason is I eventually want to make it Fair Source or Open Core, so that a hyperscaler can&#x27;t just wrap it and charge everyone (including me) a lot of money just to use it. We do have to charge money for serious production use.<p>*What if you disappear tomorrow?*<p>Absolutely valid question. That&#x27;s why I put a lot of effort into the export to SQL (eject) functionality. It&#x27;s not perfect yet, but you can export all the logic and permissions into your own Postgres database. So if you want to run it 100% standalone from Statebase, you can. The SQL export generates is ugly for now; a lot has to do with nulls. We will improve it but I wanted to avoid forcing a schema to start.<p>*AI Support?*<p>MCP is coming very soon (next few days) and x402 payments is in the works. But I wanted to get it in the hands of flesh and bone, to see if it really excites someone as much as it does me. I know it&#x27;s possible the vast majority of users will be agents, but hoping for at least a few flesh and blood champions.<p>*Plans?*<p>It&#x27;s built on Cloudflare Durable Objects for cost savings and other advantages like built-in tenant isolation and native websockets (honestly scary how well DO mapped to our needs). But it could exist anywhere. We have a node version, a desktop version (Tauri+pglite), a devvit version (Reddit games) and so on. My dream is for this to get big, very big, so anyone making a prototype experiment, throwaway or even basic production loads reach for this. We also want to hold a game jam as soon as possible and eventually I want to make one-click installer plugins for Phaser, Unity, Godot and so on. I&#x27;m going to be here all day answering questions and taking feedback, bad or good.<p>Whatever happens, I&#x27;m going to be building with it my entire life. It just &quot;feels&quot; right to me. Hope to see a lot of you on the Discord (there&#x27;s a WidgetBot on the website if you just want to leave a comment for posterity).
